From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:29:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] milkflint tests: replay recordings as the hardware

tests/replay.h plays a recording (record.h) back on top of fake.h:
register reads by address (the n-th read gets the n-th recorded value),
windows behind a selector register keyed by its value too (the remapped
registers, the A-die's SPI data register), firmware commands with the
recorded raw reply for the same command, an optional strict-order check,
and a report of what the recording doesn't cover.

The fakes now feed the recorder, so a run on them can be recorded and
replayed. fake.h gets a write hook and a hook before each firmware reply;
mt7915's fake device can take another name, for a second device in the
same test.

- mt76-record: the recorder's format, size bound, modes and firmware
  download handling, and a fake run replayed to the same code: same
  values, same replies, same recording.
- mt7915-replay: a small firmware model on the fakes runs the firmware
  boot, mt7915_init_hardware() (through the driver's own DMA firmware
  path) and all of mt7915_register_device() with its init work and
  teardown; a second device replays each recording and makes the same
  accesses (1662 for registration). These were out of the tests' reach.
  A capture from the router in the VM's
  /lib/firmware/milkflint/mt7986-capture.rec is replayed through
  registration too; without one that test is skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
